# shir_nodes/spread.node — Spread: expand a list into individual
# arguments/elements (`f(args...)` variadic spread, JS `...arr`,
# Zig/Java varargs pass-through).
#
# GENERIC. VALID ONLY where the host surface allows a spread: direct
# call arguments and collection-literal elements (ESTree restricts
# SpreadElement the same way). A frontend emitting it elsewhere gets a
# generator error — Refuse > guess at the emit layer.
#
# Relation to the existing Python-flavored `Splice` node: same runtime
# effect; Splice predates this node (Python slice-splice idiom) and
# stays for its transform consumers. New frontends should prefer this
# neutral name.

node Spread
tag "Spread"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field expr: expr
# Spec: TextOps#spread_sound (docs/fm/TextOps/ShIR_TextOps_Strings.thy, section
# "CountedFor, Spread, AddressOf/Deref, CloneDeep: value-level laws"). Spread flattens
# its operand into the argument/element vector. Proved: singletons flatten to themselves
# (spreading one-element groups is the identity); the flattened LENGTH is the sum of the
# parts' lengths; appending argument groups concatenates their flattened vectors, so order
# is preserved up to where the spread sits and a mid-list spread does not reorder its
# neighbours; and duplicate elements survive a flatten (a multiset property).
#
# NOT PROMISED (stated, not assumed): where a spread is LEGAL — ESTree's SpreadElement /
# varargs position only, with a generator error elsewhere (refuse>guess at the emit
# layer); the host's arity/type checking of the resulting call; and the evaluation order
# of the operand expression.
spec: TextOps#spread_sound
